# Force LF on every text file so the project's byte-exact integrity checks pass
# on a Windows checkout too. Several checks compare a file's raw bytes against a
# canonically re-serialized LF form -- e.g. validate_registry.py reads
# registry.v1.json with read_bytes() and requires it to equal
# json.dumps(..., indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n". Without this, Git's autocrlf
# hands Windows a CRLF checkout, the raw bytes no longer match the LF canonical
# form, and ~20 registry/source-hash assertions fail across many test files even
# though nothing about the content changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch launchers must stay CRLF to run reliably under cmd.exe.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never apply end-of-line conversion.
*.png binary
